  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively provide several relevant directions: temperature-dependent behavior in compositionally similar HEAs, evidence that diffusion need not be sluggish, element-dependent diffusion and depletion, surface-free-energy effects, kinetic control of metastable structures, and preferential Cu loss. These could motivate studying a multicomponent alloy under heating and questioning high-entropy stabilization. However, none describes in situ vacuum heating of sub-10-nm noble-metal HEA nanoparticles, surface-energy-driven Au/Cu segregation, reshaping-enhanced diffusion, or the resulting evaporation and size-distribution changes. Thus the literature points generally toward the mechanism, but selecting this nanoparticle system, intervention, and specific segregation/evaporation pathway would require a substantial new idea."
